Z||000002||Stoic||05-03-2000||10:31 PM||||hehe...thanks||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ironhorse||05-03-2000||11:16 PM||||Hey Stoic.... when you finally get around to your 6x9 set up.. please let me know how it went and give me the description of how you do it... in the near future I plan to put in 1 8 inch MTX 5000 series and Kicker 6.5 midrange speaker in the door.  A little more tricky than your would be but would like to know how you did it anyway  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Happy cutting, Fieroing, N JAMMIN!!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Stoic||05-03-2000||11:21 PM||||Ill let you know how it goes Ironhorse||||reg||12
Z||000005||Racer 1||05-04-2000||01:05 AM||||I installed 5 1/4 Kenwood speakers in my doors. <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=159982&a=1168563&p=20630822&Sequence=0" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=159982&a=1168563&p=20630822&Sequence=0</A>  . I dont think you can just plop in 6x9 mounting is to deep. My 5 1/4 I had to install a clear 1/8 lexan between the speaker and the door so the window bottom wont hit the magnet. I was thinking about making a big face plate out of wood then covering it with carpet. But there isnt much space between the seat and the door. If you have power windows you might be better of since I had to space mine so I can still row down the windows. I had a airpowered grinder and a air powered grinding wheel took me about 3 hours to install both speakers. And just a note dont drill into the doors carpet with a  drill bitt it will ripp the stands of carpet all the way up the door. My speakers sound awesome and look awesome also.||||reg||6
Z||000006||batboy||05-04-2000||10:44 AM||||Racer, what about a 4" round speaker, think that would mount in with no trouble?||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||05-04-2000||11:55 AM||||The problem is one of depth. There isn't any.<P>Bats, it will depend on the specific speaker. Racer got away with a shim. You might need one, might not, might not fit at all. depends how much the magnet is sticking off the back.<P>all,<BR>I just can't see any thing bigger than racer used fitting. you only have about 1.5-2 inches of depth all the way down the door because of the way the window works. Even less depending on just where you are working. You'd have to build up the door and I think that's gonna look really bad.<P><p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 05-04-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Racer 1||05-04-2000||12:56 PM||||Batboy im sure a 4" speaker would go in without no problems. I have 4" speakers in the rear and there way not as deep as my 5 1/4. Strange thing I found out after I had stuck in my 5 1/4 is that kenwoods 6 1/2 speakers had less mounting depth then my speakers. So I could have put in 6 1/2 instead. I think my mounting depth was 1 13/16 and that was hitting barely between the magnet and the bottom of the windows metal frame. I was going to use mirrored plexyglass and have a square mirror behind my speakers to look cool but I was in a rush to see how these babies sounded. One other thing if you do mount the speakers n the door use SIR-RAM-RAP over the back of the speakers so water wont harm the cone and spider.||||reg||10
Z||000010||1FST2M6||05-04-2000||02:31 PM||||infinity makes a 6.5" flat midbass driver. $249US pair, that will mount in 1.5" deep space... <A HREF="http://www.crutchfield.com" TARGET=_blank>www.crutchfield.com</A>  combined with a nice soft tweeter and decent cross over in your amp and she'll sound nice. <P>Stoic,<BR>London, Ontario... i was there over Thanksgiving... (Nov 26th) @ the mall...  ||||reg||1
Z||000011||jbarnes||05-04-2000||07:17 PM||||Stoic,<BR>I had to have my doors professionally modified in order to accept mine. They added a panel on the interior of the door and it looks like it's been there the whole time and sounds great!||||reg||1
Z||000012||phillip||05-05-2000||02:10 AM||||infinity also makes an 8" mid bass that is only a little over 2" deep. also try illusion audio. both are pricy but might work for you. i'm hoping to get the illusions eventually.<P>it would take some work but you could also probaly put 6x9's in the dead pedal area. a couple of us have put various sizes there and i mean to try to put 8's there in my next install (found some 8" infinity 3ways. with 2 8's in the door too that should give me enough bass)  <p>[This message has been edited by phillip (edited 05-05-2000).]||||reg||1
